From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rocket: stop the block under the job lock

rocket_job_handle_irq() writes OPERATION_ENABLE = 0 and clears the
interrupt state before it takes job_lock, while rocket_job_hw_submit()
writes OPERATION_ENABLE = 1 from inside that lock.  The two orderings are
not equivalent: a completion's zero that lands after a submit's one stops
a task the hardware has only just been given, and the job then waits out
its completion for a program that is no longer running.

The completion handler cannot race itself -- one irqaction's thread is
not re-entered concurrently -- so what opens the window here is a second
writer, and rocket_reset() is one: it is entered from
rocket_job_timedout(), which an unprivileged client reaches by pointing
drm_rocket_task.regcmd at an unmapped address, and it runs a submit path
of its own while a completion may be between its two writes.

Move both writes inside the existing scoped_guard.  Nothing else changes:
the retire path was already under the lock, and the early return for a
job with tasks left still unlocks through the guard.

Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c | 12 +++++++++---
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
index 67e4f48a5..47f1e4c70 100644
--- a/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
+++ b/drivers/accel/rocket/rocket_job.c
@@ -430,10 +430,15 @@ static void rocket_job_handle_irq(struct rocket_core *core)
 {
 	pm_runtime_mark_last_busy(core->dev);
 
-	rocket_pc_writel(core, OPERATION_ENABLE, 0x0);
-	rocket_pc_writel(core, INTERRUPT_CLEAR, 0x1ffff);
+	scoped_guard(mutex, &core->job_lock) {
+		/*
+		 * Stopping the block belongs under the lock.  rocket_job_hw_submit()
+		 * writes OPERATION_ENABLE from inside it, so this zero landing after
+		 * that one stops a task that has only just started.
+		 */
+		rocket_pc_writel(core, OPERATION_ENABLE, 0x0);
+		rocket_pc_writel(core, INTERRUPT_CLEAR, 0x1ffff);
 
-	scoped_guard(mutex, &core->job_lock)
 		if (core->in_flight_job) {
 			/*
 			 * A batched job advanced next_task_idx straight to task_count
@@ -450,6 +455,7 @@ static void rocket_job_handle_irq(struct rocket_core *core)
 			pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(core->dev);
 			core->in_flight_job = NULL;
 		}
+	}
 }
 
 static void
